---
const steps = [
  {
    title: "Tell us about the property.",
    text: "Where it is, what needs to change, and when you need to start. You don’t need a perfect scope to make the first call.",
  },
  {
    title: "Work through the details.",
    text: "Review site conditions, finish choices, access, and the work to include. These are the details that make a bid useful.",
  },
  {
    title: "Agree on the plan.",
    text: "Confirm the scope, schedule, payment terms, and how changes and final punch items will be handled before work begins.",
  },
];
---

<section class="section-padding process-section">
  <div class="container-main">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A straightforward start</p><h2>
          First, a conversation.<br />Then, a plan.
        </h2>
      </div><p>You know the property.<br />Let’s work through what it needs.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="process-grid">
      {
        steps.map((step, i) => (
          <li>
            <>
              <span class="process-number">0{i + 1}</span>
              <h3>{step.title}</h3>
              <p>{step.text}</p>
            </>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
